    "body": "New York debut. ( Image courtesy of Torex. )\nBy: Staff Writer November 19, 2026\nTorex Resources (TSX: TXR; NYSE: TXR) has won Toronto Stock Exchange approval to renew a share buyback covering about 10% of its public float, two days after the Mexico-focused miner began trading in New York.\nThe renewed bid allows Torex to repurchase up to 7.18 million common shares from Nov. 23 through Nov. 22, 2027. Under the previous authorization, which expires Nov. 20, Torex bought back 6.26 million of a permitted 8.13 million shares through Nov. 11.\nTorex began trading on the New York Stock Exchange on Tuesday, replacing its U.S. over-the-counter quotation. The company kept its primary listing in Toronto and raised no capital through the New York listing.\nThe buyback is part of Torex’s plan to return $350 million to shareholders in 2026 through repurchases and dividends. It had returned $270.8 million by Sept. 30, or about 77% of that target, the company said in its third-quarter results .\nThe company plans to fund any repurchases from available working capital. It can buy shares through the Toronto or New York exchanges or alternative trading systems in Canada and the United States. It will cancel any shares it buys.\nTSX purchases are generally capped at 129,854 shares a day, with one block purchase above that limit allowed per calendar week. Torex can suspend repurchases at any time and says its decisions will depend on market conditions, its share price and other opportunities to invest.\nPortfolio\nTorex produces gold, copper and silver at its flagship Morelos complex in Guerrero state, Mexico. The company expects first ore from Media Luna North at Morelos by year-end.\nMedia Luna. ( Image courtesy of Torex. )\nThe company, which dropped “Gold” from its name in October, is advancing a prefeasibility study for its Los Reyes gold-silver project in Sinaloa state. It holds several early-stage exploration properties in the country.\nIn Nevada, Torex holds the Medicine Springs exploration project and an option to acquire Gryphon Summit.\nPrint\nTAG: gold exploration gold mines gold mining gold production Mexico\nCOMMODITY: Copper Gold Silver\nREGION: Mexico and Central America United States\nCOMPANY: Torex Resources\nRepublish this article",
